            <ArticleTitle>Two-channel ECG monitoring in the coronary care unit.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>102-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the installation and clinical application of a two-channel monitoring system in the intensive coronary care unit using a single patient cable and two exchangeable ECG modules. Routine use of this system during a period of three years has shown that it has many advantages in the precise documentation and diagnosis of transient cardiac arrhythmias and for the recognition and localization of ischemic episodes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
